---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout title={`Radiology Legal Cases | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="Landmark decisions where radiology was central. Issue, facts and principle for each case.">
<PageHero eyebrow="Radiology Legal Cases" title="Radiology Legal Cases" description="Decisions where imaging defined breach, standard of care or consent. Issue, facts and principle." />
<section class="bg-white py-16 dark:bg-navy-900"><div class="container-page space-y-12">
<Section eyebrow="Interpretation" title="Muller v King's College Hospital [2017] EWHC 128 (QB)">
<p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Issue: perceptual error in image interpretation.</p>
<p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Facts: missed malignant melanoma on foot imaging with later expert review showing a visible lesion.</p>
<div class="card mt-4 p-6"><p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Principle: Bolam applies to judgment. It does not protect failure to see what is plainly visible to a competent radiologist. Peer evidence that others might also have missed it does not cure a perceptual miss of a demonstrable abnormality.</p></div>
</Section>
<Section eyebrow="Screening" title="Penney, Palmer and Canon v East Kent HA [2000]">
<p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Issue: standard of care in screening imaging and cytology.</p>
<p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Facts: three false negative cervical screening reports.</p>
<div class="card mt-4 p-6"><p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Principle: first question is factual. Did the slide show abnormalities. If present, failure to report or refer fell below standard. Evidence that others might have missed it was not determinative.</p></div>
</Section>
<Section eyebrow="Task standard" title="FB v Princess Alexandra Hospital [2017] EWCA Civ 334">
<p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Issue: standard for junior staff interpreting radiographs.</p>
<p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Facts: ED junior missed subtle signs with delayed treatment.</p>
<div class="card mt-4 p-6"><p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Principle: standard is set by post and task, not by seniority. A junior interpreting an X-ray is judged against a reasonably competent practitioner doing that task.</p></div>
</Section>
<Section eyebrow="Communication" title="Gwyn v South Tyneside and Sunderland [2021]">
<p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Issue: fail-safe reporting of critical findings.</p>
<p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Facts: incidental nodule suspicious for malignancy reported but not directly communicated. No alert reached the treating team.</p>
<div class="card mt-4 p-6"><p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Principle: duty extends beyond interpretation to effective communication. A report filed silently on an electronic system does not discharge duty where urgent action is required. Closed loop notification is required.</p></div>
</Section>
<Section eyebrow="Consent" title="Montgomery v Lanarkshire [2015] UKSC 11">
<p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Issue: informed consent for imaging and interventional procedures.</p>
<p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Facts: material delivery risks not disclosed.</p>
<div class="card mt-4 p-6"><p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Principle: disclosure judged by reasonable patient standard. For embolisation, biopsy and angioplasty, discuss material risks, complications and alternatives specific to that patient. Record the discussion.</p></div>
</Section>
<Section eyebrow="Categories" title="Patterns in radiology claims">
<div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2"><div class="card p-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-slate-100">System safety</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Delayed lung cancer on chest radiograph. Breach of fail-safe notification. See Gwyn.</p></div><div class="card p-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-slate-100">Fracture and spine</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Missed fracture. Cauda equina delay. ED misinterpretation. See FB.</p></div><div class="card p-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-slate-100">Interventional error</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Vascular injury. Inadequate consent. Risk disclosure failure. See Montgomery and Chester.</p></div><div class="card p-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-slate-100">Abdominal catastrophe</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Missed aortic dissection or bowel ischaemia on CT. Protocol adequacy and demonstrability decide breach. Causation requires Gregg analysis.</p></div></div>
</Section>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
